course: dictionary
lesson: 255
title: Small joining words: also
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Also» means too, or as well. It adds one more thing to what you have already said. To check, try adding «as well» or «too» in its place. If the sentence still makes sense, «also» is the right word.
explain: In «French also has many varieties around the world», the word tells you that French has many varieties in addition to whatever else the text has just said. The extra idea is that French has many forms, not just one.
explain: «Also» usually sits just before the main verb, as in «it also leaves scent». It can also start a new point, as in «Also, bring a coat», which means add this too.
explain: «Not only … but also» joins two ideas and shows that both are true. Watch for these pairs in your reading. They help you link ideas clearly in your own writing too.
fact: «Also» means too, or as well.
fact: «Also» adds one more thing or amount to what has already been said.
fact: «Also» often sits just before the main verb, as in «it also leaves scent».
fact: «Not only … but also» links two ideas, showing that both are true.
fact: «Also» can start a new point, as in «Also, bring a coat.»
exercise: In «China also gave the world porcelain, tea, kites and an early earthquake detector», what does also mean? | Only | Instead | *Too, as well | Never
exercise: Ella says «also» means «but». Which answer is right? | It means the opposite of too | *It adds one more thing, so it does not mean but | It means before | Yes, it means but, as in a contrast
exercise: In «it also leaves scent from glands in the paws», what extra idea does also add? | That blankets are soft | *That kneading leaves scent from the paws, as well as the other points | That dough needs flour | That kittens feed from their mother
test: «Charles was crowned … which was also Harry's son Archie's birthday.» What extra idea does also add? | That Westminster Abbey is in London | That Archie was crowned as King | That Harry was not there | *That the crowning day was Archie's birthday too
test: Complete the sentence: «Not only is the path steep, but it is ___ slippery.» | *also | never | instead | before
exam: Which sentence uses also to add one more thing? | Tom never likes apples, also pears. | Tom likes apples, and he likes pears instead. | *Tom likes apples, and he also likes pears.
